      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the sum of the first 10 odd positive integers, we can use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\nThe first term (a) is 1, and the common difference (d) is 2, since each odd integer is 2 more than the previous one.\n\nWe want to find the sum of the first 10 terms (n = 10), so we can use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:\n\nS_n = n/2 * (a + l)\n\nwhere S_n is the sum of the first n terms, a is the first term, l is the last term, and n is the number of terms.\n\nThe last term (l) can be found using the formula for the nth term of an arithmetic series:\n\nl = a + (n - 1)d\n\nPlugging in the values, we get:\n\nl = 1 + (10 - 1) * 2\nl = 1 + 9 * 2\nl = 1 + 18\nl = 19\n\nNow we can find the sum of the first 10 odd positive integers:\n\nS_10 = 10/2 * (1 + 19)\nS_10 = 5 * 20\nS_10 = 100\n\nSo, the sum of the first 10 odd positive integers is 100.",
